{# The running head. On an essay page the masthead scrolls away like the
   nameplate on page one, and this takes over: what you're reading, which
   issue it is, and how far through you are.

   aria-hidden, because every word in it is already announced elsewhere on
   the page — it is a visual convenience, not content. Nothing inside is
   focusable, for the same reason.

   The progress bar lives here now rather than loose at the top of the
   window, so the brass line reads as the underside of the running head.
   src/js/progress.js fills in the page count and shows the bar. #}
<div class="runhead" id="runhead" data-mins="{{ essay.readTime }}" aria-hidden="true">
  <div class="wrap">
    <span class="rh-brand">{{ site.wordmark }}</span>
    <span class="rh-no">No.&nbsp;{{ essay.number | pad }}</span>
    <span class="rh-title">{{ essay.title }}</span>
    <span class="rh-page" id="rh-page"></span>
  </div>
  <div id="progress"></div>
</div>
